@base = http://localhost:8094

### Create source
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-source

{"currency":"USD","openingBalance":1000}

> {% client.global.set("sourceId", response.body.id); %}

### Create destination
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-destination

{"currency":"USD","openingBalance":0}

> {% client.global.set("destinationId", response.body.id); %}

### Stage 1: transfer; Stage 2: re-run to replay the same transfer
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer

{"sourceId":"{{sourceId}}","destinationId":"{{destinationId}}","amount":400}

> {% client.global.set("transferId", response.body.id); %}

### Immutable balanced entries
GET {{base}}/entries

### Stage 3: reverse; re-run with the same key to replay
POST {{base}}/transfers/{{transferId}}/reversals
Idempotency-Key: demo-reversal

### Expected 409: another reversal key cannot reverse twice
POST {{base}}/transfers/{{transferId}}/reversals
Idempotency-Key: demo-duplicate-reversal

### Transfer now links to its reversal
GET {{base}}/transfers/{{transferId}}

### Rebuilt and stored balances agree
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{sourceId}}/audit

### Destination is back at 0
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{destinationId}}

### Expected 409: insufficient funds
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-overdraw

{"sourceId":"{{sourceId}}","destinationId":"{{destinationId}}","amount":1001}
